   </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;white&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> scale_fill_gradient</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">low<br>\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;white&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> high </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;black&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> name </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Absolute<br>\r\n\r\n\\nHäufigkeit&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></span></p><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><br><br>Frist I have the problem that I need to do several of this graphs and they should all have the same maxima at the legend.<br>\r\n\r\nAt the moment somtimes the top value of the legend is maybe 8 or 15 depending on the data.<br>Therefore I would like so set the scale manually to for example 15 that one can compare the graphs more easily having the same legend.<br>\r\n\r\n</div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div><br><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">​use scale_fill_gradient(limits = range(x$z, na.rm=TRUE) ...)​</div> </div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Second I would like to increase the size of the legend. I just found out that I could use &quot; <span style=\"color:blue\">+ guides(fill = guide_legend(keyheight = 3))</span>&quot; for that.<br>But if I do so the type of the legend is also changing and I would like to remain the continious gradient scale.<br>\r\n\r\n<br></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
